# kernel-c6x.img -- Linux 5.10.272 for the DSK6455 (TI C6000, run as C674x, noMMU)
#
# Runs on qemu-system-c6x -M dsk6455 from the qemu fork (lordrasmus/qemu,
# branch uclibc-ng); upstream qemu never had the C6000.  The image is the
# stripped vmlinux (ELF).
#
#   qemu-system-c6x -M dsk6455 -m 256M -nographic -kernel kernel-c6x.img \
#     -initrd rootfs.img.xz -append 'console=ttyS0 lpj=500000'
#
# The machine follows arch/c6x/boot/dts/dsk6455.dts and generates the
# device tree itself.  The real board's console went through the JTAG
# emulator, so the tree adds an NS16550A at 0x02b80000 (SERIAL_8250_OF),
# and a syscon at 0x02bc0000 with syscon-poweroff: poweroff ends qemu.
# The CPU is a C674x rather than the C6455's C64x+, so that the floating
# point code of the uClibc-ng toolchain runs.
#
# 5.10 is the last line with c6x (removed in v5.11).
#
# Patches, each one fix, against linux-5.10.272:
#   kernel-c6x-sync-file-range.patch  sync_file_range read its offsets from
#                                     registers the syscall entry does not
#                                     pass on
#   kernel-c6x-tls.patch              GPLYB, the thread pointer of the C6000
#                                     EABI, follows the task across context
#                                     switches and clone sets it with
#                                     CLONE_SETTLS (kernel built with gas'
#                                     -mno-tp-gplyb, see the binutils patch)
#   kernel-c6x-user-gie.patch         start_thread left GIE off for init,
#                                     whose registers come from a kernel
#                                     thread, and every program inherited
#                                     it, so user code was never preempted
#
# Build: kernel-c6x.config is dsk6455_defconfig with SERIAL_8250(_CONSOLE),
# SERIAL_OF_PLATFORM, SERIAL_EARLYCON, NR_UARTS 1, MFD_SYSCON,
# POWER_RESET_SYSCON_POWEROFF, DEVTMPFS(_MOUNT), BINFMT_FLAT, PRINTK_TIME,
# NET, INET, UNIX, PACKET, POSIX_MQUEUE and FUTEX.
#
# -m 256M: the default 128 MB is too little for the NPTL test rootfs.
#
#   cd linux-5.10.272
#   for p in kernel-c6x-sync-file-range.patch kernel-c6x-tls.patch \
#            kernel-c6x-user-gie.patch; do patch -p1 < $p; done
#   cp kernel-c6x.config .config
#   make ARCH=c6x CROSS_COMPILE=tic6x-openadk-uclinux- olddefconfig vmlinux
#   tic6x-openadk-uclinux-strip -o kernel-c6x.img vmlinux
#
# The toolchain is the CI's toolchain-c6x-c674x-gcc-7.5.0-lt-shared-nommu-dsbt.
#
# Known: without lpj= the delay loop calibration takes very long under
# qemu; the cause is not tracked down yet.
